p) vs\n    `len ∈ 10…15` (no `lookup` write); `s == NULL` (dist tree, no `lookup`\n    memset) vs `s != NULL` (lit tree).\n14. `cp_decode` binary search shapes: 1-symbol tree, 2-symbol tree, full\n    288-symbol tree, and trees whose `first[15]` (`max_index`) is < the symbol\n    count.\n15. The 7 writable tables: unmodified vs. modified through the `.so` export.\n16. Empty output (`EOB` as the first symbol), 1-byte output, ≥64 KiB output.\n\n## Rows (each row = one differential test configuration, randomized inputs)\n\n| # | entry point(s) | configuration (options set + input shape) | [ ] |\n|---|----------------|------------------------------------------|-----|\n| 1 | `pinflate` | `first_bytes=0`, `last_bytes=0`, single fixed block, random literals | [ ] |\n| 2 | `pinflate` | `first_bytes=0`, `last_bytes=1` | [ ] |\n| 3 | `pinflate` | `first_bytes=0`, `last_bytes=2` | [ ] |\n| 4 | `pinflate` | `first_bytes=0`, `last_bytes=3` | [ ] |\n| 5 | `pinflate` | `first_bytes=1`, `last_bytes=0` | [ ] |\n| 6 | `pinflate` | `first_bytes=1`, `last_bytes=1` | [ ] |\n| 7 | `pinflate` | `first_bytes=1`, `last_bytes=2` | [ ] |\n| 8 | `pinflate` | `first_bytes=1`, `last_bytes=3` | [ ] |\n| 9 | `pinflate` | `first_bytes=2`, `last_bytes=0` | [ ] |\n| 10 | `pinflate` | `first_bytes=2`, `last_bytes=1` | [ ] |\n| 11 | `pinflate` | `first_bytes=2`, `last_bytes=2` | [ ] |\n| 12 | `pinflate` | `first_bytes=2`, `last_bytes=3` | [ ] |\n| 13 | `pinflate` | `first_bytes=3`, `last_bytes=0` | [ ] |\n| 14 | `pinflate` | `first_bytes=3`, `last_bytes=1` | [ ] |\n| 15 | `pinflate` | `first_bytes=3`, `last_bytes=2` | [ ] |\n| 16 | `pinflate` | `first_bytes=3`, `last_bytes=3` | [ ] |\n| 17 | `pinflate` (`cp_stored`) | one stored block, `LEN = 0`, `in_bytes` chosen so `bits_left/8 == LEN` | [ ] |\n| 18 | `pinflate` (`cp_stored`) | one stored block, `LEN = 1` | [ ] |\n| 19 | `pinflate` (`cp_stored`) | one stored block, `LEN ∈ 2…4096` random, all 4 `in` alignments | [ ] |\n| 20 | `pinflate` (`cp_stored`) | one stored block, `LEN = 65535` (max), `out_bytes == LEN` | [ ] |\n| 21 | `pinflate` (`cp_stored`) | stored block, `out_bytes < LEN` (no `out_end` check in C ⇒ deliberate overflow into the padded out buffer) | [ ] |\n| 22 | `pinflate` (`cp_fixed`/`cp_block`) | fixed block, EOB only (empty output), `out_bytes = 0` | [ ] |\n| 23 | `pinflate` (`cp_fixed`/`cp_block`) | fixed block, literals only: all 256 byte values, plus random | [ ] |\n| 24 | `pinflate` (`cp_fixed`/`cp_block`) | fixed block, literal symbols including the 9-bit range (144…255) and 8-bit range | [ ] |\n| 25 | `pinflate` (`cp_block`) | fixed block, every length symbol `257…285` × min/mid/max extra-bit value, distance symbol 0 (`dist=1`, `memset` path) | [ ] |\n| 26 | `pinflate` (`cp_block`) | fixed block, every distance symbol `0…29` × min/mid/max extra-bit value, length 3 | [ ] |\n| 27 | `pinflate` (`cp_block`) | fixed block, length symbols `286`, `287` ⇒ `cp_len_base == 0` ⇒ length 0, followed by a distance symbol (0-byte copy) | [ ] |\n| 28 | `pinflate` (`cp_block`) | fixed block, distance symbols `30`, `31` ⇒ `cp_dist_base == 0` ⇒ `backwards_distance == 0`, `src == dst` (no-op copy of `length` bytes) | [ ] |\n| 29 | `pinflate` (`cp_block`) | fixed block, `backwards_distance == 1` (`memset` path) with length 3…258 | [ ] |\n| 30 | `pinflate` (`cp_block`) | fixed block, overlapping copy `1 < distance < length` (byte loop, forward propagation) | [ ] |\n| 31 | `pinflate` (`cp_block`) | fixed block, `distance == length`, and `distance > length` | [ ] |\n| 32 | `pinflate` (`cp_block`) | fixed block, `distance` exactly equal to the bytes emitted so far (`out - distance == begin`, boundary of E4) | [ ] |\n| 33 | `pinflate` (`cp_block`) | fixed block, match ending exactly at `out_end` (boundary of E5) | [ ] |\n| 34 | `pinflate` (`cp_block`) | fixed block, ≥64 KiB output built from long matches (distance up to 32768) | [ ] |\n| 35 | `pinflate` (`cp_dynamic`) | dynamic block, `HLIT=257`, `HDIST=1`, `HCLEN=19`, direct code lengths only | [ ] |\n| 36 | `pinflate` (`cp_dynamic`) | dynamic block, `HLIT=288`, `HDIST=32`, `HCLEN=19`, random complete trees | [ ] |\n| 37 | `pinflate` (`cp_dynamic`) | dynamic block, `HCLEN` swept `5…19` (each value that can still describe the tree) | [ ] |\n| 38 | `pinflate` (`cp_dynamic`) | dynamic block using code-length symbol `16` (repeat previous, extra 0…3) | [ ] |\n| 39 | `pinflate` (`cp_dynamic`) | dynamic block using code-length symbol `17` (3…10 zeros) | [ ] |\n| 40 | `pinflate` (`cp_dynamic`) | dynamic block using code-length symbol `18` (11…138 zeros) | [ ] |\n| 41 | `pinflate` (`cp_dynamic`) | dynamic block using 16/17/18 mixed, `n` landing exactly on `nlit+ndst` | [ ] |\n| 42 | `pinflate` (`cp_dynamic`) | dynamic block with all code lengths ≤ 9 (⇒ `cp_build` fills `lookup`) | [ ] |\n| 43 | `pinflate` (`cp_dynamic`) | dynamic block with code lengths in 10…15 (⇒ `cp_build` skips `lookup`) | [ ] |\n| 44 | `pinflate` (`cp_dynamic`) | dynamic block, literal tree = single symbol 256 with length 1 (under-subscribed, `max_index == 1`) | [ ] |\n| 45 | `pinflate` (`cp_dynamic`) | dynamic block, distance tree with exactly 1 symbol (`HDIST=1`, length 1) and matches | [ ] |\n| 46 | `pinflate` (`cp_dynamic`) | dynamic block, distance tree with 2 symbols, lengths {1,1} | [ ] |\n| 47 | `pinflate` (`cp_dynamic`) | dynamic block, `cp_permutation_order` fully exercised: all 19 code-length slots non-zero | [ ] |\n| 48 | `pinflate` (`cp_dynamic`) | dynamic block, random complete trees × all 4 `in` alignments × all 4 `last_bytes` | [ ] |\n| 49 | `pinflate` (`cp_dynamic`) | dynamic block, matches using all length/distance symbols reachable from the random tree | [ ] |\n| 50 | `pinflate` | `out_bytes` exactly the decompressed size (all block types) | [ ] |\n| 51 | `pinflate` | `out_bytes` larger than needed, and `out_bytes = INT_MAX` | [ ] |\n| 52 | `pinflate` | `out` unaligned (offsets 0…7 into the padded buffer) | [ ] |\n| 53 | `cp_fixed_table` + `pinflate` | rotate the fixed literal/distance code lengths into another *valid* complete pair of trees, then decode a fixed block | [ ] |\n| 54 | `cp_fixed_table` + `pinflate` | swap the 7-bit and 8-bit groups (still a complete tree) | [ ] |\n| 55 | `cp_len_base` + `pinflate` | change `cp_len_base[0]` (length of symbol 257) to another value ⇒ different copy length | [ ] |\n| 56 | `cp_len_extra_bits` + `pinflate` | change `cp_len_extra_bits[0]` from 0 to 3 ⇒ 3 extra bits consumed for symbol 257 | [ ] |\n| 57 | `cp_dist_base` + `pinflate` | change `cp_dist_base[0]` from 1 to 4 ⇒ different backwards distance | [ ] |\n| 58 | `cp_dist_extra_bits` + `pinflate` | change `cp_dist_extra_bits[0]` from 0 to 5 | [ ] |\n| 59 | `cp_permutation_order` + `pinflate` | reverse the permutation table and encode a dynamic block accordingly | [ ] |\n| 60 | `cp_error_reason` + `pinflate` | pre-set to a non-null value, then run a *successful* stream ⇒ must stay untouched | [ ] |\n| 61 | `pinflate` | 2 blocks: stored → fixed (`bfinal` on the 2nd) | [ ] |\n| 62 | `pinflate` | 2 blocks: fixed → stored | [ ] |\n| 63 | `pinflate` | 2 blocks: dynamic → fixed, matches crossing the block boundary (`begin` is the whole out buffer, not the block start) | [ ] |\n| 64 | `pinflate` | 2 blocks: fixed → dynamic, second block re-builds `lit`/`dst`/`lookup` | [ ] |\n| 65 | `pinflate` | 3 blocks: stored → dynamic → stored | [ ] |\n| 66 | `pinflate` | N∈{1..6} random blocks of random types, random data, × alignments (property test, 512 seeds) | [ ] |\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":20,"oldLines":7,"newStart":20,"newLines":7,"lines":[" `cp_fixed`, `cp_decode`, `cp_dynamic`, `cp_block`, `cp_make_pixel`,"," `cp_make_pixel_a`) have internal linkage and cannot be called across the FFI"," boundary, so \"lowest level first\" here means: drive each of them directly through","-the smallest bit-stream that reaches it, and через the writable tables they read","+the smallest bit-stream that reaches it, and through the writable tables it reads"," — which is what the rows below do (rows 1–16 are pure bit-reader / `cp_ptr` /"," `cp_peak_bits` coverage, 17–24 `cp_build`+`cp_decode` via the fixed tree, 25–40"," `cp_dynamic`, 41–52 `cp_block` copy paths, 53–60 the writable tables, 61–66"]}],"userModified":false,"replaceAll":false}}
