{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_zps2ujygducfpfluf633pqckzicqa3w4v33iut6wyfjfatp7olja","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Verification is complete. All four phases pass.\n\n## What was verified\n\nThe library is `pinflate` — a DEFLATE decompressor (cute_png's inflate) — exporting one function and seven **mutable** data tables.\n\n**Phase A artifacts** (in `translation/`), all derived mechanically from `c_src/src/lib.c`:\n- `SYMBOLS.md` — all 8 exported symbols; `nm -D` diff is **empty** (names, kinds, and data-object sizes all match), for both the debug and release cdylib.\n- `ERRORS.md` — 24 rows: the 6 `cp_error_reason` branches, all 10 `assert()` sites, and 8 generic FFI boundaries.\n- `CONFIGS.md` — 70 valid-input rows across 16 axes (input-pointer alignment × `in_bytes % 4`, all 3 block types and their orderings, all 29 length symbols, all 30 distance symbols, `HLIT`/`HDIST`/`HCLEN` extremes, all repeat codes, both copy paths, all six writable tables…).\n\n**Phases B–D**: `tests/differential.rs` loads *both* `.so`s via `libloading` and compares, per case: return value, the `cp_error_reason` **string**, the whole *padded* output allocation (so out-of-range writes are caught), the exported tables, and — for inputs that kill the process — the signal plus **byte-exact stderr**.\n\n**16 082 cases × 2 profiles, 0 failures.**\n\n## Findings\n\n- **No behavioural divergence was found** — the translation was already faithful. Every initial test failure was my own `Expect` prediction being wrong, not a C/Rust mismatch.\n- Two real fixes/hardenings to the Rust:\n  - `build.rs` now reproduces the C `__FILE__` (CMake compiles by absolute path), so `assert` failures print byte-identical messages instead of `src/lib.c:…`.\n  - 18 `.offset()` calls that legitimately go out of bounds (`tree[-1]`, `out + out_bytes` with a negative `out_bytes`, the final-word read at `in + in_bytes - last_bytes`, table indices from corrupt Huffman symbols) became `wrapping_offset` — same addresses, but no longer UB that LLVM could exploit where gcc `-O0` cannot.\n- I corrected my own analysis in `ERRORS.md`: `cp_ptr`'s `assert(!(s->bits_left & 7))` is **reachable** (the `cp_peak_bits` final-word fold breaks the alignment invariant); a hand-built 6-byte stream triggers it in both libraries identically. A2/A5/A7 are proved unreachable, with the proofs recorded.\n- Exhaustively swept **all 65 536 two-byte inputs** and all 1-byte inputs × 4 alignments: 48 880 abort identically with matching assert text.\n- `cp_sweep_random` found 2 inputs on which `cp_dynamic` **never terminates** (its repeat codes overwrite the low byte of `n` on the stack). Both libraries hang on exactly those two and still hang after 45 s — the Rust's emulated gcc stack frame, which I verified against `objdump -d`, reproduces this.\n- One honest limit is documented in `ERRORS.md` §D: nine uninitialised padding bytes in `cp_dynamic`'s C frame are zero in the emulation; they're only readable via an execution that the same clobbering makes non-terminating.\n\nRun everything with `translation/run_verification.sh` (~2.5 min; `PINFLATE_FULL_SWEEP=1` adds the exhaustive 2-byte sweep)."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":508,"cache_read_input_tokens":414226,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":508,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ff3766ed-9021-4a97-b413-26636dbe17c8","uuid":"27fd2a4a-f05c-4cdf-9b64-eb01d4b92b37","timestamp":"2026-08-27T16:08:30.930Z"}
